        Croatia's legal framework for remote workers is established under the <em>Foreigners Act</em> (<em>Zakon o strancima</em>, Official Gazette Nos. 133/20, 114/22, and 151/23). Rather than imposing an arbitrary fixed monetary benchmark that depreciates with inflation, the Croatian Parliament dynamically linked the digital nomad financial threshold directly to the nationwide average net monthly salary calculated annually by the Croatian Bureau of Statistics (<em>Državni zavod za statistiku - DZS</em>).
      </p>
