      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        Bank Statement Standards &amp; Forensic Police (MUP) Audit Requirements
      </h2>
      <p>
        The administrative body evaluating digital nomad applications is the Croatian Ministry of the Interior (<em>Ministarstvo unutarnjih poslova - MUP</em>), operating through regional police directorates (<em>policijska uprava</em>) in cities such as Zagreb (Petrinjska 30), Split (Trg Hrvatske bratske zajednice 8), and Dubrovnik. Immigration inspectors reject approximately 22% of initial submissions due to non-compliant financial documentation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Adhere strictly to the four forensic validation pillars enforced by MUP officers:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-4 text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5">
        <li>
          <strong>Consecutive 6-Month Chronology</strong>: You must provide official monthly statements covering the uninterrupted six months immediately preceding your filing date. A single closing balance snapshot is insufficient; the officer verifies cash-flow continuity and consistent foreign client remittances.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Digital Security Signatures &amp; Direct Bank Exports</strong>: Statements must be direct electronic PDF exports containing the issuing bank's cryptographic digital certificate or an ink stamp accompanied by a branch manager's signature. Screenshots of mobile banking apps, spreadsheet reconciliations, and third-party accounting printouts are instantly disqualified.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Eligible Account Classifications</strong>: Personal checking accounts, individual savings accounts, and business accounts belonging to single-member LLCs (where the applicant demonstrates 100% beneficial ownership via Articles of Incorporation) are acceptable. <strong>Cryptocurrency cold wallets, public blockchain addresses, stock brokerage equity portfolios (Interactive Brokers/Robinhood), and locked retirement pensions (US 401k/IRA) are strictly excluded</strong> because they do not represent guaranteed immediate liquidity.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>FX Conversion &amp; Buffer Margin</strong>: For statements in USD, GBP, CAD, or AUD, MUP converts closing balances into Euros utilizing the official daily midpoint exchange rate published by the Croatian National Bank (<em>Hrvatska narodna banka - HNB</em>). If currency volatility drops your balance below €2,539.31 on the exact day of review, your file will be paused or denied. Always maintain a 10% cash buffer.
        </li>
      </ul>

